Subject: fix(cli): resolve the agents repo on the configured host in dispatch and lint

Patch 0005 moved fullsend run's agents-repo fallback onto the configured
forge. Three later readers of the same fallback still assume github.com:

- `fullsend dispatch --route`, which reusable-dispatch.yml runs for every CEL
  route, resolves the agent's harness with a bare gh.New(""). On any other
  forge the lookup fails, the harness role cannot be read, and the route's
  authorization threshold fails closed to write without saying the harness
  was never found.
- `fullsend lint` builds the same fallback client with a bare gh.New.
- The offline cache scan and the dispatch decision label match cached URLs
  against defaultAgentsRepoURLPrefix, while the online path now pins them
  under agentsRepoRawURLPrefix(). Offline, a harness the previous run cached
  on an enterprise forge is never found.

Use newGitHubLiveClient for both clients, which honours GITHUB_API_URL and
keeps the token optional, and match against agentsRepoRawURLPrefix() in both
scans. github.com keeps the public prefix, so behaviour there is unchanged.

Breadboard note: patches Go source, so it belongs to the build patch list in
deploy/scripts/05i-build-fullsend.sh. Found while rebasing the patch set onto
v0.52.0: these call sites were added upstream after 0005 was written. Written
to be sent upstream as-is, alongside 0005. Add a DCO sign-off before
submitting it as a human-authored change.

